{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_fe3985eac801601b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"bonsai2-27b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed. The bug is on line 7: `while start < end` is exclusive, but the README contract requires counting **both** endpoint dates (inclusive). Let me trace the failing behavior:\n\n- `test_same_weekday`: same date → loop never runs (`start < end` false) → returns 0, expected 1. **Fails.**\n- `test_week`: Mon–Fri inclusive = 5, but exclusive loop only counts Mon–Thu = 4. **Fails.**\n\nThe fix is a single character: `<` → `<=`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"cache_creation":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":2199,"inference_geo":null,"input_tokens":447,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":578},"server_tool_use":{"web_fetch_requests":0,"web_search_requests":0},"service_tier":null},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e10801ff-3722-4577-a7a5-789253245961","uuid":"34c4b2da-30d5-458b-b595-ed85ce64f4fe","timestamp":"2026-11-03T11:20:08.012Z","request_id":"msg_fe3985eac801601b"}
