{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_d698b08f2fad8a7a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"bonsai2-27b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 4 tests pass. Here's the summary:\n\n## What was wrong\n\nThe README contract states `business_days` counts **both** endpoint dates (inclusive). But the loop in `schedule.py` used `while start < end`, which is exclusive — it never counted the final `end` date. This caused:\n- `test_same_weekday`: same-date range → loop never ran → returned 0 instead of 1\n- `test_week`: Mon–Fri counted only Mon–Thu → returned 4 instead of 5\n\n## The change\n\nA single-character fix on line 8 of `schedule.py`:\n\n```python\n# before\nwhile start < end:\n# after\nwhile start <= end:\n```\n\nThis makes the loop iterate through and include the `end` date, satisfying the inclusive contract. No other logic (weekday check, holiday filtering, reversed-range `ValueError`) was touched.\n\n## Actual test result\n\n```\ntest_holiday ... ok\ntest_reversed ... ok\ntest_same_weekday ... ok\ntest_week ... ok\n\nRan 4 tests in 0.000s\nOK\n```\n\nAll 4 tests pass. I did not modify `test_existing.py` or `README.md`, and no dependencies were installed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"cache_creation":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":3033,"inference_geo":null,"input_tokens":141,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":20},"server_tool_use":{"web_fetch_requests":0,"web_search_requests":0},"service_tier":null},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e10801ff-3722-4577-a7a5-789253245961","uuid":"fb4d8848-c3d4-427a-9a86-07d3d9d37c13","timestamp":"2026-11-03T11:20:12.833Z","request_id":"msg_d698b08f2fad8a7a"}
